      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1161431479,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 255885252,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795783156837,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Notes\n· snapd's built-in slots: on Core the system exposes them implicitly. The Session snap's display-manager, user-session and document-portal plugs are super-privileged and store-gated.\n· wayland, x11, desktop: upstream snapd has no built-in slot for them on Core, so the session snap must expose them (as Ubuntu Frame does). The prototype plugs wayland instead.\n· The Driver assistant installs pc-kernel components and driver snaps through snapd; the target doc doesn't name its interface yet.\n· Connections come only from store declarations: the stock pc gadget has no desktop connections (target-architecture §3.2).",
      "originalText": "Notes\n· snapd's built-in slots: on Core the system exposes them implicitly. The Session snap's display-manager, user-session and document-portal plugs are super-privileged and store-gated.\n· wayland, x11, desktop: upstream snapd has no built-in slot for them on Core, so the session snap must expose them (as Ubuntu Frame does). The prototype plugs wayland instead.\n· The Driver assistant installs pc-kernel components and driver snaps through snapd; the target doc doesn't name its interface yet.\n· Connections come only from store declarations: the stock pc gadget has no desktop connections (target-architecture §3.2).",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b60",
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
